          %title
          %p
            Xiao-Gang Wen is a professor in theoretical physics at MIT. His expertise is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter"} condensed matter
            theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+correlated+system"} strongly correlated
            electronic systems and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
            and its
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+protected+topological+phase"} symmetry proteced
            versions. Topological orders also classify finite generalized symmetries in one lower dimensions.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://xgwen.mit.edu/"} personal homepage
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://physics.mit.edu/faculty/xiao-gang-wen/"} Institute page
                at MIT
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xiao-Gang_Wen"} Wikipedia entry
          %p
            Interview on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Ball"}> Philip Ball
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Making the world from topological order
              %strong 6
              2 (2019) 227–230
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/nsr/nwy116"} doi:10.1093/nsr/nwy116
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Introducing and developing the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vacuum Degeneracy of Chiral Spin State in Compactified Spaces
                %strong 40
                7387 (1989) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.40.7387"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.40.7387
                ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological Orders in Rigid States
                %strong 4
                239 (1990) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217979290000139"}> doi:10.1142/S0217979290000139
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://xgwen.mit.edu/sites/default/files/documents/topo.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                , Qian Niu:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ground state degeneracy of the FQH states in presence of random potential and on high genus Riemann surfaces
                %strong 41
                9377 (1990) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.41.9377"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.41.9377
                ]
            %li#Wen91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-Abelian statistics in the fractional quantum Hall states
                %strong 66
                (1991) 802 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.802"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.802
                )
            %li
              %p
                E. Keski-Vakkuri,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"} Xiao-Gang Wen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ground state structure of hierarchical QH states on torus and modular transformation
                %strong 7
                4227 (1993) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217979293003644"}> doi:10.1142/S0217979293003644
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9303155"} arXiv:hep-th/9303155
            %li#Wen93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Topological order and edge structure of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ν
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu = 1/2
                    quantum Hall state
                %strong 70
                (1993) 355
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.70.355"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.70.355
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li#Wen95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological orders and Edge excitations in FQH states
                %strong 44
                (1995) 405
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9506066v2"} arXiv:cond-mat/9506066v2
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00018739500101566"} doi:10.1080/00018739500101566
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p Early review:
          %ul
            %li#Wen91Review
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological orders and Chern-Simons theory in strongly correlated quantum liquid
              %strong 05
              10 (1991) 1641-1648 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217979291001541"}> doi:10.1142/S0217979291001541
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The additional requirement that the Berry connection be non-abelian (and/or the presence of anyons):
          %ul
            %li#GuWen09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zheng-Cheng+Gu"}> Zheng-Cheng Gu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"} Xiao-Gang Wen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor-Entanglement-Filtering Renormalization Approach and Symmetry Protected Topological Order
              %strong 80
              155131 (2009) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0903.1069"}> arXiv:0903.1069
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.80.155131"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.80.155131
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Zoo of quantum-topological phases of matter
              %strong 89
              41004 (2017) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.03911"}> arXiv:1610.03911
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.89.041004"} doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.89.041004
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+spin+liquids"} quantum spin liquids
            as exhibiting
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Wilczek"} Frank Wilczek
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Zee"} Anthony Zee
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chiral spin states and superconductivity
              %strong 39
              (1989) 11413 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.39.11413"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.39.11413
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+effect"} fractional quantum Hall effect
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"}> Xiao-Gang Wen
